MediaWorkflowConfiguration create and update are
synchronous reread flows. OCI returns the body
immediately and the resource exposes only ACTIVE
and DELETED, so the reviewed runtime does not
publish provisioning or updating lifecycle
buckets.
The published runtime excludes isLockOverride
from update and delete, so lock overrides stay
out of scope for the controller-backed surface.
Delete confirmation treats either a DELETED
lifecycle reread or OCI NotFound as terminal; a
reread that still returns ACTIVE after delete is
treated as delete pending and keeps the
finalizer until OCI stops returning the
resource.
Matching create-time locks are normalized by
ignoring OCI-populated timeCreated metadata so
steady-state reconcile does not fail after a
successful create that requested locks, but
omitting spec.locks later still counts as
create-only drift while OCI reports locks.
Promotion to a seeded formal row is deferred to
the convergence story that updates
manifest-owned catalog metadata.
end note
